<section class="tale-hero" id="top"><div class="tale-hero-copy"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/index.html">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/stories.html">Stories</a><span>/</span><span>Bhramari Devi and Aruna</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">SRIMAD DEVI BHAGAVATA PURANA / BOOK TEN</p><h1>The Mother who commanded<br><em>the countless bees.</em></h1><p class="tale-deck">Aruna's extraordinary boon seems to place heaven beyond rescue. The Devas turn to the Divine Mother, who appears as Bhramari and reveals what his power has overlooked.</p><div class="tale-meta"><span>Devi Bhagavata Purana · 10.13.33–127</span><span>About {{ storyCatalog.bhramari.minutes }} min read</span><a href="/sources.html#bhramari-aruna">View sources</a></div><a class="button" href="#narada-question">Begin the story</a></div><figure class="tale-hero-art"><img src="/assets/images/bhramari-manifestation.png" alt="Bhramari Devi appears amid shining clouds and innumerable dark bees before astonished Devas, as imagined in cinematic artwork" width="1200" height="900" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>THE MOTHER APPEARS BEFORE THE DEVAS</figcaption></figure></section>
<div class="tale-introduction"><p>From the <strong>Srimad Devi Bhagavata Purana, Book 10, Chapter 13</strong>. Narayana answers Narada's question about Bhramari Devi and the fall of the Daitya Aruna. This original English prose retelling follows the owner-supplied Swami Vijnananda translation without reproducing its passages verbatim.</p></div>
<section class="story-characters" aria-labelledby="characters-title"><p class="eyebrow">MEET THE CHARACTERS</p><h2 id="characters-title">Characters in this story</h2><dl><div><dt>Bhramari Devi</dt><dd>The World Mother manifesting with innumerable bees, offering refuge and overcoming Aruna's forces.</dd></div><div><dt>Aruna</dt><dd>A male Daitya who performs severe penance, obtains a restrictive boon and seizes the heavens.</dd></div><div><dt>Brahma</dt><dd>The creator who appears after Aruna's austerities and grants the qualified boon.</dd></div><div><dt>Indra and the Devas</dt><dd>The displaced celestial powers who seek aid from the Divine Mother.</dd></div><div><dt>Brihaspati</dt><dd>The preceptor sent by Indra to confront Aruna's reliance on his austerities.</dd></div><div><dt>Narayana and Narada</dt><dd>The sage narrating Bhramari's episode and the listener who asks about her manifestation.</dd></div></dl></section>
